# ORION Phase 10D — Boundary Specification

Version: 1.0

Status: Architecture Boundary Lock

---

# Purpose

This document defines the operational boundaries of every subsystem introduced during Phase 10D.

Its objective is to preserve the architectural principles established throughout ORION by preventing responsibility leakage between modules.

Every module has clearly defined permissions.

Everything outside those permissions is explicitly forbidden.

These boundaries are mandatory and must remain enforced throughout all future development.

---

# Global Architecture Rules

The following rules apply to every subsystem introduced during Phase 10D.

## Rule 1

The frontend never performs autonomous decision making.

---

## Rule 2

The frontend never computes operational plans.

---

## Rule 3

The frontend never performs optimization.

---

## Rule 4

The frontend never allocates resources.

---

## Rule 5

The frontend never modifies Digital Twin runtime state directly.

All state mutations must occur through existing Intent APIs.

---

## Rule 6

The Digital Twin remains the single runtime source of truth.

---

## Rule 7

Mission execution remains entirely under backend control.

---

## Rule 8

Planning algorithms remain backend responsibilities.

