# Validation Requirements

Every future implementation under Phase 10D shall validate:

* Boundary compliance
* Forbidden import scan
* Dependency validation
* Architecture validation
* Type validation
* Manual workflow validation
* Documentation synchronization

Any boundary violation shall block progression to the next phase.

---

# Final Boundary Statement

Phase 10D extends the ORION operational workflow without altering the architectural responsibilities established in previous phases.

No subsystem receives additional authority outside its defined responsibility.

Mission Planning prepares missions.

The backend plans missions.

Hive orchestrates missions.

HAL abstracts hardware.

The Digital Twin reflects reality.

Mission Control visualizes reality.

Every subsystem has a single responsibility, a single owner, and a clearly defined boundary.

These boundaries are considered locked from the completion of Phase 10D onward and shall remain the foundation for all commercial development beginning in Phase 11.
